\f1\b\fs28 ATA Design Rationale FAQ\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 1. Platform Redirection & Navigation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 FAQ: How does training redirection work from iata.org to Store?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What happens when a user selects a training course on iata.org?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  When a user selects a training from the training list on iata.org, they are automatically redirected to the corresponding training detail page hosted within Store.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  Will users remain on iata.org during the training purchase flow?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  No. After selecting a training, users are redirected from iata.org to Store, where the next steps are managed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  Why are users redirected to Store?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  Store is the dedicated platform for purchase.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 FAQ: Why do the return button labels change across the experience?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  When is the \'93Go back to shopping\'94 label used?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  The \'93Go back to shopping\'94 label is used only when the user originally entered the experience through the shopping flow.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What happens in all other navigation scenarios?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  In all other cases, the button label defaults to \'93Go back\'94 only.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  Why does the return label change dynamically?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  The label adapts based on the user\'92s entry point to provide clearer navigation context and more accurate return paths.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 FAQ: Why is the \'93Go back to shopping\'94 action removed after purchase of an physical item?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  Why is the \'93Go back to shopping\'94 button removed from the confirmation screen after purchasing a physical item?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  After physical item purchase completion, the experience shifts focus from shopping to post-purchase actions and confirmation-related next steps. In this case, the main CTA is to Go back to shopping, hence the secondary on the top of the screen is removed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What replaces the \'93Go back to shopping\'94 action?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  The confirmation experience prioritizes post-purchase primary actions relevant to the completed transaction, making additional shopping actions secondary.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 2. Dynamic Call-to-Action Logic\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 FAQ: Why does the CTA label change on the training detail page on Store?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  Why does the primary CTA label change from \'93Register\'94 to \'93Add to Cart\'94 on the training detail page on Store?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  
\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 The CTA changes to 
\f4\b \'93Add to Cart\'94
\f3\b0  because trainings are now treated consistently with other Store products. Previously, training used 
\f4\b \'93Register\'94
\f3\b0  and redirected users to the LMS. With the updated experience, users can add trainings directly to the cart and continue the purchase journey.
\f0 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  Does the CTA behavior depend on the user\'92s status or eligibility?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  Yes. The CTA behavior dynamically changes based on the user\'92s eligibility, authentication state, and training requirements. That can either be \'93Add to Cart\'94 or \'93Apply\'94. \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What happens if a training has prerequisites?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  If a training includes prerequisites, the primary CTA changes to \'93Apply\'94 for logged-out users or users who do not yet meet the eligibility requirements.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What does an eligible logged-in user see when viewing training with prerequisites?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  If the user is logged in and eligible, they see \'93Add to Cart.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 3. Authentication & Account Recognition\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 FAQ: How does the email recognition and login flow work?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  How does the email recognition and what happens after a user enters their email address?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  The system checks whether the entered email address is already associated with an existing account.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What happens if the email address is recognized?\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A:
\f0\b0  If the email already exists in the system, the user is prompted to enter their password and sign in.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Q:
\f0\b0  What happens if the email address is not recognized?\
